      "side": 1,
      "message": "Marked as unresolved.\n\nThis avoids repeating message multiple times, but AFAIK it does not save flash space actually (If I\u0027m wrong, please share the numbers).\n\nInitially I was thinking about moving `LOG_ERR()` to `elan_spi_transaction_*()` functions, but you will lose information about function that called `elan_spi_transaction_*()`.\n\nYou could do something like\n```\nstatic const char *spi_write_fail_msg \u003d \"spi_write FAILED: in func: %s with retval \u003d %d\\n\";\n```\nand use it in LOG_ERR(), but I\u0027m not sure if it looks good for you.",
